## Key finding

The premise of the appended instruction did not hold in this container: **dsh-migrate did not migrate anything.** Its own evidence says why:

- `/logs/agent/agent.log` → `the repository holds no plugin: no package.json that declares dsh.bundle, at its root or below it`
- `/logs/agent/status.json` → `{"migrations": []}`
- `git -C /app diff HEAD -- fixture` → empty; `/tmp/dsh-migrate-bench/pipeline-output/` → empty (no `migrations/0.1.2-alpha.2/`, no `cards.json`, reviews, repair/patch reports or event log)
- Code path: `findPlugins()` requires `'bundle' in dsh` and the walk skips dot-directories, so `.dsh-plugin/package.json` (`dsh.entry`) is invisible — a discovery gap, not a compatibility finding.

I did **not** modify `/app/fixture` (harness instruction; the report is the deliverable per the skill's landing-discipline rule). Instead I diagnosed the gap and **verified the full migration recipe end-to-end on a disposable copy** with an isolated `DSH_HOME`:

- `dsh plugin --profile web add` → bundle stack gains `@demo/dsh-bench-repo`; `--dump-config` shows the row
- cold boot → token URL 303 + Cookie → `__DSH_BOOT__.entries` contains the package id → advertised bundle 200 (910 B, `__ModuleLoader__.load`)
- real Chromium: `#bench-pet` = 🐋 mounted in `BODY`, no page errors; legacy `/pet/ui.js` → 404
- negative control: a plain-ESM `client.js` fails with `SyntaxError: Unexpected token 'export'` / *loaded without registering* — so the client half must be a `__ModuleLoader__.load({ id, factory })` bundle whose factory exports `{ name, apply }`
- pre-existing failure isolated under R-06: `dsh --profile web` crashes on this image after printing its URL (`user patch-layer watching requires the Cordis HMR service`), reproduced on a fresh home with no plugin

